    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span><span class=\"time\">30 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip warn\">Medium</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Sliding window</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Fixed window frequency match</span>\n    <a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/permutation-in-string/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 567</a>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Permutation in String</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">A permutation of s1 is any string with exactly s1's letter counts, and it has s1's length. So slide a window of length len(s1) over s2 and ask \"do the counts match?\". Keep one diff array and a counter of how many of the 26 letters agree: each slide changes two counters, and the check is O(1). O(n1 + n2) time, O(26) space.</p>\n"
  },
